Feature: Physical presets sound like the records they were written for
  The physical-guitar presets of the seventh round were each written for a kind of record. A
  corpus of the user's own records (197 tracks in 29 groups) was separated with htdemucs_6s and
  its guitar stems measured; tests/tone_reference.hpp holds the numbers (no audio), generated by
  tools/tone_gate_profiles.py. tests/tone_features.hpp measures exactly as the corpus analysis did,
  checked against it on fourteen stems with tools/tone_measure.cpp (agreement to rounding).
  The corpus has since grown (play-count groups; The War on Drugs and Portugal. The Man, 341
  tracks in 41 groups); tests/tone_reference.hpp is regenerated from it, and each added group's
  presets join the same scenario.

  Groups whose separation the corpus analysis found unreliable (the Olivia Tremor Control's
  records, the Beatles') are not gated against that corpus, and neither are presets for kinds of record the corpus
  has none of (jazz archtop, classical, the singing-sustain lead).

  The presets written for lo-fi 4-track and home-recorded psychedelic records answer to a second,
  six-stem corpus (14 lo-fi tracks, 12 home-psych tracks; htdemucs_6s, all six stems measured by
  song-corpus/scripts/features.py). tests/stem_reference.hpp holds its numbers (no audio),
  generated by tools/stem_gate_profiles.py; tests/stem_features.hpp measures as that script does,
  pYIN tape wobble included, checked against it on every gated render (agreement to rounding).
  A preset is judged as the stem it would be separated into, inside the group's plain
  interquartile range. Not gated: the lo-fi group's bass and other stems (near-empty on most of
  those records), share of mix (a mixing decision, not a sound), and the bass stem's wobble (pYIN
  starts at 65 Hz, so a bass line's low notes pin to its floor and read as no wobble at all).

  Executable: tests/tone_gate_tests.cpp (CTest tone_gate_tests).

  # each_records_preset_sounds_like_the_records
  Scenario: Each records preset sounds like the records
    Given each physical preset written for a group of records, playing sixteen seconds in that style at 120 BPM
    Then its centroid, 85% roll-off, share above 3 kHz, spectral flatness, 100 ms crest and L/R correlation each land within the group's quartiles widened by 0.75 IQR
    And its third-octave shape from 100 Hz to 8 kHz lies within 4 dB on average of the group's median shape

  # each_stem_preset_lands_in_its_groups_quartiles
  Scenario: Each stem preset lands in its group's quartiles
    Given each preset written for the lo-fi or home-psych records' guitar, bass or other stem, playing sixteen seconds of its part at 120 BPM
    When it is measured as that stem
    Then its centroid and 85% roll-off lie inside the group's interquartile range
    And a guitar's L/R correlation does too
    And a guitar's or other stem's tape wobble, in cents, does too

  # the_master_tape_machine_puts_tape_wobble_on_any_source
  Scenario: The master tape machine puts tape wobble on any source
    Given a physical guitar playing droned chords, and a combo organ holding chords, with the master tape machine's wow and flutter off
    When the machine's flutter is turned to 55%
    Then the measured wobble rises from under 2.5 cents to over 4 cents, by more than 2.5
